    "turn_idx": 344,
    "turn_text": "or and then try to kind of soften the consequences of it. And that is defined by the people that we send to represent us that outcome. But I do think that people respond and elected officials respond to those incentives, as you mentioned, not only do are they responsive to sunlight, your money isn't the only rule here. At the end of the day, people who are in Congress want to return to Congress. And it's true. And then the reason. And the reason that the Republicans have so much enforcement is because they're more scared of a primary than they are of a general",
